# golangci-lint release pinned by CI and `make lint`: <version> <go-built-with>.
#
# The second field is the Go version the release binary was compiled with, which
# is also the newest Go it can analyse. golangci-lint refuses to run when go.mod
# targets a newer Go than that — most often because a `toolchain` line was added
# as a side effect of running `go get` / `go mod tidy` under a newer local
# toolchain. Keeping the version and this Go field together, and checking them
# against go.mod, is what scripts/check_lint_toolchain.sh does; see
# CONTRIBUTING.md#lint-toolchain-drift.
